From 3f8a43754af08af7b4eee8ec69eec3289d351e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:53:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] P5c: TR-143 DownloadDiagnostics and
 UploadDiagnostics, 26 parameters

Ported from functions/tr143/download_diagnostic and upload_diagnostic;
the transfers stay in DownloadDiagnostics_launch / UploadDiagnostics_launch.

TR-143 stops differently from every other diagnostic: the data model
never kills.  downloadDiag_stop_diagnostic() queues "<launcher> stop" on
the apply-service list when DiagnosticsState is Requested, so the order of
the queue decides what runs after the session ("Requested" then
"DownloadURL" in one SPV queues "run &" then "stop").  Kept, call for call;
icwmp applies an SPV in order (set_list_tmp, list_add_tail, FIFO).

Vendor bug kept: uploadDiag_stop_diagnostic() reads the state with
$UCI_SET_VARSTATE_UPLOAD.  "uci set x.y.z" without a value fails
(uci list.c:702 UCI_ASSERT(ptr->value)), -q hides it, so the Upload
setters never queue a stop.

Quirks kept: http/ftp only, the URL must equal what grep -o prints (and
so "" is accepted); Interface reads "" when unset; EthernetPriority is
option EthPriority; TestFileLength has no upper bound; the *Time leaves
are strings reading 0000-00-00T00:00:00.000000 before the first run.

dmmtk: mtk_grep_o() -- "$(echo "$s" | grep -E -o re)".
diag_mtk: download/upload stores, diag_stop_queued(), diag_queue_run(),
diag_url_valid().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
